# Ledger row #2 — I/O, L1 — HDF5 scalar-attribute hoist
# File: pecan/dataset.py, Dataset_PDB.__init__ (h5-driven path) + __getitem__
# Verdict: KEPT, but NOT credited as an independent performance win —
# measured +3.3% mean vs baseline (within noise, 3 replicates, CV 1.8%),
# but 0 correctness regressions, so left in place as groundwork for opt1.
#
# Mechanism: moves the 5 scalar bond-count attribute reads
# (num_hbonds/hpbonds/habonds/sbonds/pbonds) from __getitem__ (executed once
# per sample PER EPOCH) to __init__ (executed once per sample TOTAL, at
# dataset construction). __getitem__ then reads these values from data_list
# instead of touching h5_data.attrs on every call.

